WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.170
- One of the things you spoke about

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:04.510
during the pandemic was keeping
track of our mental health.

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:06.120
And we touched on it a bit here.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.690
How is your mind doing through everything?

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.740
Mine has been a rollercoaster!

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.822
- Yeah, it's definitely
been a roller coaster.

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:15.216
You know, I've been very open and vocal

00:00:15.216 --> 00:00:17.592
about growing up with
mental health challenges,

00:00:17.592 --> 00:00:20.910
and that that's a continuing issue

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.950
for many of us who struggle.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.100
Also, the notion that
it's okay to not be okay.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.170
That's some of the messaging that NAMI,

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.365
the National Alliance on Mental Illness

00:00:29.365 --> 00:00:32.702
tries to really spread the word about.

00:00:32.702 --> 00:00:37.702
I'm not gonna sugar coat it,
it's been incredibly taxing

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.070
for many of us, especially those
of us who struggled before.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.680
I'm an introvert by nature, which means

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.822
I don't mind being on my own
and not really going out a lot.

00:00:45.822 --> 00:00:46.970
- Yeah.
- But the notion

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:48.890
that that's being chosen for me--

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.540
- Yeah, the option has been ripped, yeah.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.400
- Yeah, it can feel really isolating.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.190
And you know, my temper's been short.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:58.640
My sleep's been weird, I started
getting heart burn again.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.840
Just like all the stress things.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.790
But those are all stress
things for my body.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:05.600
And also, I was talking with a girlfriend,

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.890
and even my lady cycle
has felt more emotional

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.430
during the quarantine, like
everything is heightened.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.410
And my mom has a pinched
nerve in her back.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.560
She never had that before.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.590
And I said, we're all stressed.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.340
We're living in masks, we don't
know what tomorrow brings.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.030
The news is insane, the country's

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.740
falling apart it feels like.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.630
It's very stressful, even for someone

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:27.330
who has zero history
with mental health stuff.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:28.898
And for those of us who have OCD,

00:01:28.898 --> 00:01:31.670
there's plenty of things
to have new obsessions

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.360
and compulsions about, I promise (laughs).

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.512
- I know, definitely,
it's been a rollercoaster.

00:01:37.512 --> 00:01:39.010
I have suffered from depression.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:39.940
And it's like one of those things

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:41.500
where I don't do well,
and I'm an extrovert,

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.725
so this like not seeing
humans and not interacting,

00:01:44.725 --> 00:01:48.160
I like really feed off of people's energy.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:48.993
- Yeah.

00:01:48.993 --> 00:01:50.411
- And I love the people that I've chosen

00:01:50.411 --> 00:01:52.130
to surround myself with in my life.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.380
So yeah, I've definitely missed

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.115
even like my glam squad, you know?

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.350
I don't miss glam, I love what they do,

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.840
but I don't miss the
hour of sitting there.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.700
But I miss them and I
miss talking to them,

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.100
and I think all of us are like that

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.223
with work and stuff--
- Well, and you can

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:07.080
only do so many Zoom
meetings, you know (laughs)?

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:07.913
- Yeah.

00:02:07.913 --> 00:02:08.960
- You can only do so much.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.378
And even socializing, it's not the same,

00:02:11.378 --> 00:02:13.370
and you have to use
your voice differently,

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:14.630
and you have to worry what I look like,

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:16.850
and I end up just like staring
at myself the whole time,

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:18.040
and like why do I look like that?

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.270
That's not helpful either.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:20.810
- Yeah, I don't even do that.

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.160
I just never look (laughs).

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.770
That's the key, just don't look.

